{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/HashFunc","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"typealias","externalID":"s:4GLib8HashFunca","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Type Alias","title":"HashFunc","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HashFunc"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HashFunc","kind":"identifier"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HashFunc"},{"text":" = ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GHashFunc","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GHashFunc"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The function is passed a key and should return an ","type":"text"},{"code":"unsigned int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hash value."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The functions [func"},{"code":"direct_hash","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"int_hash"},{"type":"text","text":"] and [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"str_hash"},{"type":"text","text":"] provide"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hash functions which can be used when the key is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"void*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"int*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"char*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" respectively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direct_hash"},{"type":"text","text":"] is also the appropriate hash function for keys"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of the form "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"conversion-macros.html#gint-to-pointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(or similar macros).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A good hash functions should produce"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"hash values that are evenly distributed over a fairly large range.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The modulus is taken with the hash table size (a prime number) to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"find the ‘bucket’ to place each key into. The function should also","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be very fast, since it is called for each key lookup."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that the hash functions provided by GLib have these qualities,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but are not particularly robust against manufactured keys that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cause hash collisions. Therefore, you should consider choosing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a more secure hash function when using a [struct","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/HashTable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] with keys"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that originate in untrusted data (such as HTTP requests).","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Using [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"str_hash"},{"type":"text","text":"] in that situation might make your application"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vulnerable to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/lwn.net\/Articles\/474912\/"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key to choosing a good hash is unpredictability.  Even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cryptographic hashes are very easy to find collisions for when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remainder is taken modulo a somewhat predictable prime number.  There","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"must be an element of randomness that an attacker is unable to guess."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Specifies the type of the hash function which is passed to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HashTable.new"},{"type":"text","text":"] when a [struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/HashTable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] is created."}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/hashfunc"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/HashTable":{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/HashTable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" struct is an opaque data structure to represent a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"data-structures.html#hash-tables"},{"type":"text","text":". It should only be accessed via the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"following functions.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HashTable"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HashTable"}],"title":"HashTable","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/hashtable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/HashTable"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/HashFunc":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/hashfunc","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Specifies the type of the hash function which is passed to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text